rts2-base (0.1.0-3) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * debian/control, debian/rules: split the FLI (Finger Lakes
    Instrumentation) drivers out of rts2-base into a new binary package,
    rts2-drivers-fli (rts2-camd-fli, rts2-focusd-fli, rts2-filterd-fli).
    Built from the same source/same dpkg-buildpackage run - no extra
    compilation - but keeps rts2-base itself buildable on a host without
    the (non-redistributed) vendor libfli SDK; on such a host
    rts2-drivers-fli just comes out empty rather than failing the build.
    gxccd stays in rts2-base for now (not asked to split, and unlike FLI
    it's a single driver with no separate focuser/filter siblings).

 -- RTS2 Project <petr@rts2.org>  Mon, 20 Jul 2026 23:35:00 +0200

rts2-base (0.1.0-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * packaging/rts2.ini: set [observatory] base_path explicitly to
    /var/lib/rts2/images/ (rts2-db's postinst creates and owns this
    directory). The code default of "/images/" when unset is root-owned
    and unwritable by the "rts2" user rts2-executor runs as - found via a
    live install where image writes were silently failing (no error
    logged - see the matching fitsfile.cpp fix). Only affects fresh
    installs of this conffile; existing customized rts2.ini files are
    untouched by design (standard conffile handling) and need the line
    added by hand.
  * kernel/src/fitsfile.cpp: FitsFile::createImage() logged an error on
    every failure path except mkpath() failing - added the missing
    logStream() call so a bad image base path fails loudly instead of
    silently.

 -- RTS2 Project <petr@rts2.org>  Mon, 20 Jul 2026 00:05:00 +0200

rts2-base (0.1.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial rts2-base package: core (centrald, wire protocol, rts2-mon)
    plus every statically-linkable driver family from the base CMake
    port (dummy, D50/SBT/FRAM mounts and domes, focusers, filter wheels,
    sensors, FLI and gxccd cameras). Excludes Andor (vendor SDK ships
    only a shared library, no static option) and Paramount (libmks3
    source is under an informal non-redistribution understanding, not
    vendored into this build).

 -- RTS2 Project <petr@rts2.org>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 18:03:23 +0200
